I was trying to do something like this:
SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = 'John' OR name = 'john';
Wait, why did it not work? I thought I had it right. Maybe I missed a comma or a semicolon. The query just kept failing. I spent hours trying to figure out what was wrong with it. And then it hit me – maybe the syntax was off. I remember reading somewhere that SQL is fickle like that. But I was determined to make it work. I kept tweaking it, adjusting the clauses, trying every permutation I could think of. And still, it wouldn't run. It was like
